From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Johansen <john.johansen@canonical.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Mar 2026 00:15:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] UBUNTU: SAUCE: apparmor5.1.0 [23/25]: apparmor: skb: fix
 apparmor_secmark_check() when !inet and secmark defined.

BugLink: http://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2142956

apparmor_secmark_check() was only designed to work with inet/inet6
packets, and it relies on the presence of the secmark to indicate the
packet is inet/inet6. However this is no longer correct.

Instead of making apparmor_secmark_check() work with non-inet/inet6
packets that have a secmark. Check that the packet is inet/inet6
before proceeding.

Fixes: ab9f2115081a ("apparmor: Allow filtering based on secmark policy")
Signed-off-by: John Johansen <john.johansen@canonical.com>
Signed-off-by: Paolo Pisati <paolo.pisati@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00241
Ledger-Origin: ubuntu@bae621aa9489baba51c5eee1234884177073b36a
---
 security/apparmor/lsm.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/security/apparmor/lsm.c b/security/apparmor/lsm.c
index 3be032f4bb12..45cb9437a0a5 100644
--- a/security/apparmor/lsm.c
+++ b/security/apparmor/lsm.c
@@ -1879,6 +1879,8 @@ static int apparmor_socket_sock_rcv_skb(struct sock *sk, struct sk_buff *skb)
 
 	if (!aa_secmark() || !skb->secmark)
 		return 0;
+	if (sk->sk_family != PF_INET && sk->sk_family != PF_INET6)
+		return 0;
 
 	/*
 	 * If reach here before socket_post_create hook is called, in which
